{%- comment -%}
  The competition ticker.

  A thin moving strip at the very top of the page whose only job is to show a
  visitor, before they have scrolled or decided anything, that there is real
  golf kit here and what an entry costs.

  EVERYTHING IN IT IS REAL. Each item is one open competition from a real
  collection, carrying that product's own title and its own Shopify price, and
  linking to its own page. There is nothing to hard-code and nothing to invent:
  with no open competitions the section renders nothing at all, because a
  ticker scrolling past an empty catalogue is worse than no ticker.

  WHY IT IS NOT A COUNTDOWN.

  Movement here is navigational, not temporal. It exposes more competitions
  than fit on one line; it does not tick towards anything, does not change
  colour, and does not speed up. Nothing in it implies that waiting costs the
  visitor something. That distinction is the whole reason this is acceptable
  in a brand that bans countdown timers.

  ACCESSIBILITY AND MOTION.

    - prefers-reduced-motion turns the animation off and leaves a strip the
      visitor can scroll themselves, rather than freezing it and hiding the
      items that were off-screen.
    - It pauses on hover and on keyboard focus, so a moving target never
      escapes a pointer or a tab stop.
    - Every item is a real link with its own accessible name.
    - The duplicate track that makes the loop seamless is aria-hidden and
      removed from the tab order, so the list is announced once, not twice.
    - The wrapper clips its own overflow, so a track wider than the viewport
      can never scroll the page sideways.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign collection = collections[section.settings.collection]
  assign limit = section.settings.items_to_show | default: 8

  comment
    Only competitions a visitor can actually enter. A sold-out competition in
    a promotional strip is an advert for a dead end.
  endcomment
  assign open_items = ''
-%}

{%- capture items_markup -%}
  {%- for product in collection.products limit: limit -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Only competitions Shopify will actually sell. A sold-out competition is
      excluded because the strip is promotional and an advert for something
      that cannot be bought is a dead end. A passed closing_at is NOT a reason
      to exclude: the competition is still purchasable, so hiding it would
      conceal something the customer can still enter.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if product.available -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          Most competition titles already begin "Win a ...". Prefixing those
          again would read "Win a Win a TaylorMade Qi10 Driver", so the prefix
          is only added when the title does not already carry it.
        endcomment
        assign lower_title = product.title | downcase
        assign already_win = false
        if lower_title contains 'win a ' or lower_title contains 'win the ' or lower_title contains 'win an '
          assign already_win = true
        endif

        if already_win
          assign win_text = product.title
        else
          assign win_text = 'products.competition.ticker_win' | t: title: product.title
        endif

        assign price_text = product.price | money
        if product.price_varies
          assign price_text = product.price_min | money
        endif
        assign price_line = 'products.competition.ticker_price' | t: price: price_text
      -%}
      <li class="ticker__item">
        <a class="ticker__link" href="{{ product.url }}" data-track="ticker_click">
          <span class="ticker__prize">{{ win_text | escape }}</span>
          <span class="ticker__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span class="ticker__price num">{{ price_line }}</span>
          <span class="ticker__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span class="ticker__cta">
            {{- 'products.competition.enter_now' | t -}}
            {%- render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-right', size: 12 -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- assign open_items = open_items | append: 'x' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- assign open_count = open_items | size -%}

{%- if open_count > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    One loop of the track should take roughly the same time per item however
    many there are, so a single competition does not crawl and eight do not
    race. The duration is the item count times a per-item seconds setting.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign duration = open_count | times: section.settings.seconds_per_item -%}

  {% style %}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .ticker { --ticker-duration: {{ duration }}s; }
  {% endstyle %}

  <div class="ticker ticker--{{ section.settings.colour_scheme }}" data-ticker>
    <div class="ticker__viewport">
      <ul class="ticker__track" role="list">
        {{ items_markup }}
      </ul>
      {%- comment -%}
        The second copy is what makes the loop seamless: each track translates
        by its own full width, at which point copy two sits where copy one
        started.

        It is decorative duplication, so it is hidden from assistive technology
        and taken out of the tab order. `inert` does both in current browsers,
        but where it is unsupported a link inside an aria-hidden container is
        still reachable by keyboard -- a tab stop that announces nothing and
        moves while you are on it. Every anchor in the clone therefore carries
        its own tabindex="-1" as well, rather than relying on the container.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign clone_markup = items_markup | replace: '<a class="ticker__link"', '<a tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" class="ticker__link"' -%}
      <ul class="ticker__track" role="none" aria-hidden="true" inert>
        {{ clone_markup }}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Competition ticker",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-ticker",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A moving strip of the competitions that are open right now, taken from a collection. Each item shows that competition's real title and price. With no open competitions the strip does not render at all."
    },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Collection" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "items_to_show",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Maximum competitions",
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "seconds_per_item",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 16,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "s",
      "label": "Seconds per competition",
      "info": "How long one competition takes to cross the strip. Higher is slower and calmer.",
      "default": 9
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "colour_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colour_scheme",
      "options": [
        { "value": "deep", "label": "Deep green" },
        { "value": "brand", "label": "Brand green" }
      ],
      "default": "deep"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Competition ticker" }]
}
{% endschema %}
